  faqs: [
    { question: "Where do I even start looking for an IB tutor in Ichalkaranji?", answer: "Start by telling us the programme, subject, level and exam session your child is on, and we build a shortlist from that alone. Since no Ichalkaranji school actually teaches the IB, we search on syllabus fit nationwide rather than trying to find someone nearby, then fit the lesson time around your evenings. Nothing gets decided before a free trial class, and we swap the tutor out if it does not click." },
    { question: "Is Cambridge IGCSE tutoring available for students in Ichalkaranji?", answer: "It is, delivered online rather than through a visit to your home. The curriculum itself is what VIBGYOR High in Kolhapur teaches, the closest confirmed school, roughly 29 kilometres from Ichalkaranji. We match by the actual code and tier, whether that is Mathematics 0580 Extended or Chemistry 0620, and build sessions around Cambridge's real past papers and mark schemes." },
    { question: "Will an IB Gram tutor actually come to our house in Ichalkaranji?", answer: "No, nobody visits the house here. That kind of in-person arrangement exists only in Gurugram and pockets of Delhi NCR. Everywhere else, Ichalkaranji included, teaching happens live, one to one, over video with a shared digital whiteboard, which is real online tuition rather than a doorstep promise we cannot keep." },
    { question: "What should I budget for IB or IGCSE tutoring in Ichalkaranji?", answer: "It depends mainly on the programme, subject, level and how scarce a tutor for that exact syllabus is nationally, and we put the number in writing for your specific match before the trial. Diploma HL subjects generally cost more than Cambridge IGCSE Core work. Travel never enters the fee since every session is online, and nothing here locks you into a fixed term." },
    { question: "Does any school in Ichalkaranji actually run IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Not at present. Podar International School carries the CBSE syllabus despite its name, and no other Ichalkaranji school has authorised IB status or a verified Cambridge or Edexcel link. VIBGYOR High in Kolhapur, about 29 kilometres away, is the nearest confirmed Cambridge option." },
    { question: "My son or daughter boards at an IB school away from Ichalkaranji. Can tutoring still help over the holidays?", answer: "Very much so, and it is one of the requests we hear most from this city, since nothing local teaches the Diploma or Middle Years Programme. We match a tutor to the exact subject, level and syllabus the boarding school follows, and build sessions around school breaks or, where allowed, quiet evening slots during term." },
    { question: "Do you let us try a class before paying anything?", answer: "Always. A free trial class opens every match, working a genuine topic from your child's own syllabus over video, with nothing charged and no obligation to carry on. Afterward the tutor writes up a short plan for the first month, and you decide whether to continue, tweak it, or ask for someone different." },
    { question: "Will a tutor write or fix up my child's IB Internal Assessment?", answer: "No, that line stays firm. What a tutor will do is help narrow down a workable research question, unpack what an assessment criterion is really asking for, talk through data collection, and give straight feedback on drafts. Producing or rewriting the assessed work itself breaches IB integrity rules, so our tutors decline it outright." },
    { question: "Which Diploma subjects can Ichalkaranji families get help with?", answer: "Coverage runs across the main Diploma groups: Maths Analysis and Approaches and Applications and Interpretation at HL and SL, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, along with Theory of Knowledge and the Extended Essay, matched to whatever a boarding student from Ichalkaranji is actually taking." },
    { question: "Do you also cover MYP and PYP, or only the Diploma years?", answer: "The full continuum is covered. For Ichalkaranji families this usually means PYP support built around reading, writing and number confidence, and MYP support that unpacks the lettered assessment criteria properly while keeping the Personal Project on schedule, all for children attending an IB school elsewhere." },
    { question: "With no IB school nearby, can online lessons really replace one?", answer: "For most families, yes, given that Ichalkaranji has no local IB school and only a single confirmed Cambridge option within reach. A shared screen, live worked examples and past-paper marking cover almost everything a classroom would, and the trade-off is a far wider pool of subject specialists than the city could ever offer on its own." },
    { question: "How does IB Gram check a tutor before introducing them?", answer: "Qualifications, recent teaching of that exact subject and level, and how they approach assessment criteria all get checked before any introduction. Because Ichalkaranji's own school base for either curriculum is so thin, we specifically look for tutors who have taught the current syllabus rather than a generalist, and the trial class lets you judge the rest." },
    { question: "What is the right age or grade to begin tutoring here?", answer: "Beginning at the start of the course gives the most room to work with, Class 11 for the Diploma or Grade 9 for IGCSE, since foundations, IA deadlines and predicted grades all follow close behind. Starting later still helps, though the plan narrows toward the highest-value topics and past papers before the exam series." },
    { question: "We are considering moving our child from the State Board to IGCSE. Is that something a tutor handles?", answer: "Yes, and it comes up often, usually around Grade 9 when families are weighing VIBGYOR High or a school further afield. The real adjustment is rarely the content; it is command words like 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify', which need direct teaching well before the switch actually happens." },
    { question: "Can we schedule around Ichalkaranji's own festival and work calendar?", answer: "Yes, this gets planned for rather than left to chance. Summer heat pushes many families toward earlier evening slots, and Ganpati and Diwali, along with heavier monsoon weeks, shift routines enough that we build lighter schedules around them instead of losing sessions unexpectedly. A second weekly slot before mocks is easy to add." },
    { question: "What if the tutor turns out to be the wrong fit?", answer: "Tell us, and we arrange someone else. Families hear from us every few weeks regardless, and a re-match happens whenever the fit genuinely is not working rather than asking a child to push through it. Nothing here runs on a fixed contract, so pausing or stopping costs nothing either." },
    { question: "Does IB Gram have any formal tie to schools in or near Ichalkaranji, or to the exam boards?", answer: "None at all. IB Gram operates independently, with no affiliation to Podar International School, VIBGYOR High, the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education, or Pearson Edexcel. Schools appear on this page purely to describe where families around Ichalkaranji actually study, and tutors work to each one's own calendar and syllabus." },
  ],

